    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec requires that a created owner exposes a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`. The `AcceptanceTest` creates an owner via `POST /api/owners`, reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, and asserts `$.displayName == \"<lastName>, <firstName>\"`.\n\nTwo changes, both in the existing DTO layer (no new OfficeFloor functions needed since the responder already maps the entity through `OwnerMapper`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped it from the stored names on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause `displayName` is derived in the mapper from the persisted `firstName`/`lastName`, it appears consistently on both the create response and subsequent GETs. Full test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
